  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe document now holds shared tool components, and each tool can hold a component stack. A change to one shared component updates each tool that uses it, in one undo step.\n\n- `crates/app/src/schema.rs`: two new schema components.\n  - `DocumentComponents` is a world singleton. It has one row (`DocumentComponent`) for each component id. A row keeps the #3642 `ToolComponent` and the #3643 `ComponentGeometry` together.\n  - `ToolAssembly` sits on a tool entity. It is the stack: for each node, a component id and its `Mount`.\n- `crates/app/src/tool_assembly.rs`: reads and writes the table and the stacks, lists the users of a component (`users_of`), and derives a tool (`derive`) with the #3643 resolver.\n- `crates/app/src/commands/tool_assembly.rs`: four undoable commands (below).\n- `ChangeTool::assembled`: every `ChangeTool` law, with the body law judged against the body that lands in the same step.\n- `DeleteTool` keeps the stack and restores it on undo. It moved to `commands/tool_delete.rs`, so that `commands/tool.rs` stays under 400 lines.\n- Review fix 1: the generic `DeleteEntity` (the tree's delete) also restores the stack on undo. The two delete paths now snapshot and land one shared list, `ToolRecords` (`commands/tool_delete.rs`): the record, the number, the body, the cutter and the stack. A search found no other path that deletes a tool and restores it (the tool import's replace mode uses `DeleteTool`).\n- The project loader clears the table, so that no row of the previous document leaks into the next one.\n- Review fix 2: `NewDocument` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`) clears the table too, next to the units, machine and post resets.\n- `camcraft_app` re-exports `component`, `component_geometry` and `connection_code` of `camcraft_tools`, so that a caller outside `app` can make a table row. This adds no crate dependency.\n\n## The commands and their refusals\n\n| Command | Does | Refuses by name |\n|---|---|---|\n| `UpsertDocumentComponent` | Adds a row. A held id goes through `EditDocumentComponent`. | Each edit refusal, for a held id. |\n| `EditDocumentComponent` | Replaces a row. Derives each tool that uses it again. Lands the table, each `ToolDef` and each `ToolBody` in one undo step. | An id that the document does not hold; an edit equal to the row; each `derive` or `ChangeTool` refusal of any user tool, with the component id and the tool name. Nothing changes. |\n| `DeleteDocumentComponent` | Deletes an unused row. | An unknown id; a used component (names the tools). |\n| `SetToolAssembly` (`new`, `clear`) | Sets a stack and lands the derived records in one undo step. `clear` removes the stack and keeps the records. | No such tool; an unknown component id; each #3642 fit and #3643 resolver refusal; a body in the flutes; each `ChangeTool` law; a lathe-held tool. |\n\nOperations go Stale by their stamps: the tool record and `tool_body::digest` are in each stamp. No command writes a status.\n\n## Readings\n\n- An insert edit from `CCMT09T304` to `CCMT09T308` changes the corner radius of the Ø25 and the Ø32 cutters from 0.4 mm to 0.8 mm. The diameters stay 25 mm and 32 mm. The two Face operations go Stale.\n- A `DCMT11T304` in the CC seats is refused: `the edit of tool component 'insert-cc' is refused: tool 'Fly25': assembly: ... does not fit ...`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nIn `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/assembly_cmds.rs` (joins the `tool_library_holders` suite):\n\n- `one_shared_insert_edit_updates_two_assemblies_in_one_undo_step`\n- `an_edit_one_assembly_cannot_take_is_refused_whole_by_name`\n- `a_used_component_is_not_deleted_and_an_unused_one_is`\n- `an_incompatible_stack_is_refused_by_name_and_changes_nothing`\n- `set_tool_assembly_lands_the_derived_tool_and_body_in_one_undo_step`\n- `a_deleted_tool_comes_back_with_its_stack`\n- `review_generic_delete_undo_keeps_assembly` (review fix 1: delete through `DeleteEntity`, undo, the stack is back, and a shared edit updates the tool again)\n\nIn `crates/ui/tests/machine.rs` (next to `new_document_retires_the_machine_with_the_rest`):\n\n- `new_document_clears_the_component_table` (review fix 2)\n\nThe two review pins fail on `7ce62c040` and pass on the new head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The turning insert of the issue. The resolver has only the spindle side (#3643 is open for the lathe side). The tests use a milling insert in two indexable cutters. `derive` refuses a lathe-held tool by name.\n- A solid cutting item through the commands. The resolver pins of #3643 cover it, and `derive` uses the solid tool's own record.\n\n## What is left\n\n- #3645: the table and the stacks in `.camproj` and `.camtools`, the user library, `library_ref`. Today the derived `ToolDef` and the drawn body save; the stack and the table do not.\n- #3647: the MCP tools for the four commands (`MCP: <command>` follow-up). This PR adds no MCP tool.\n- #3648: the UI. It also decides how a hand edit (`ChangeTool`, `SetToolBody`) and a stack live together. Today the next component edit derives the records again.\n- #3646: the full `Tool` record of a multi-seat cutter. Today an insert gives the diameter and the corner radius only.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3644-component-commands.md`.\n\n## Gate\n\nAll on the final head `8fd0a47ec3519947a09f3ca78c650b882ff72d05` (log: first line is the head SHA):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 304 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The plan includes `app suites: tool_library_holders` (16 passed), `ui suites: machine` (8 passed) and `example_catalog`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The two review pins fail on `7ce62c040` (source fix held back, tests kept) and pass on the new head.\n\nP6: no heavy step.\n\nChangelog: Tool components: the document holds shared tool components, and a tool can be built from a component stack. An edit of one component updates every tool that uses it in one undo step, and their operations go Stale. A delete of a used component and a stack that does not fit are refused by name.\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #3644\n\n\n",
